    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list of everything that happens when you `POST /api/owners`, based on `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:743`).\n\n## Before the method body runs\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`. Caller must hold `OWNER_ADMIN`, else **403**.\n2. **Bean Validation on the `@Valid OwnerFieldsDto` body** (framework-enforced, \u2192 **400** via `handleMethodArgumentNotValidException`):\n   - `firstName`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `lastName`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `title`: `@Size(max 30)`\n   - `address`: `@Size(1..255)`; `addressLine1`: `@Size(1..255)`; `addressLine2`: `@Size(max 255)`\n   - `city`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email`: `@Size(1..255)`, `@Email`\n   - `postcode`: `@Pattern(^[0-9]{4}$)`\n   - `registrationDate`, `birthDate`: `@Valid`\n\n## Inside the method, in execution order\n\n3. **Idempotency short-circuit** \u2014 reads `Idempotency-Key` header; if seen before, returns the existing owner with **200 OK** and does nothing else.\n4. **Address normalization** (`applyAddress`) \u2014 trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET`/`RD\u2192ROAD`/`AVE\u2192AVENUE`; prefers `addressLine1/2` over flat `address`; writes normalized values + composed `address` back to the DTO. *(side-effect: mutates DTO)*\n5. **Required-field check** (`validateRequiredFields`) \u2014 non-blank `firstName`, `lastName`, `address` (composed), `city`, `telephone`; else `RequiredFieldsMissingException` \u2192 **400**.\n6. **Registration date handling** \u2014 null \u2192 `today`; future date \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` **400**; then `toBusinessDay` rolls weekends/2026 public holidays forward. Written back to DTO. *(side-effect)*\n7. **Daily-owner-limit** (`rejectDailyOwnerLimit`) \u2014 scans all owners; if \u2265 100 already registered that date \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException` \u2192 **429**.\n8. **City-capacity** (`rejectCityAtCapacity`) \u2014 scans all owners; if \u2265 50 in that city \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` \u2192 **409**.\n9. **Postcode validation** (`validatePostcode`) \u2014 must be `\\d{4}`; if city maps to a region (Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD) the postcode must fall in that region's range; else `InvalidPostcodeException` \u2192 **400**.\n10. **Telephone normalization** (`normalizeTelephone`) \u2014 strip separators, force E.164 (default `+61`, drop leading 0), enforce 8\u201315 digits and country-specific national length (+61\u21929, +1\u219210); else `InvalidTelephoneException` \u2192 **400**. Written back to DTO. *(side-effect)*\n11. **Email normalization** (`normalizeEmail`) \u2014 blank\u2192null; else must match email regex, lower-cased, and rejected if the domain is disposable (mailinator/tempmail/guerrillamail); else `InvalidEmailException` \u2192 **400**. Written back to DTO. *(side-effect)*\n12. **Household id + duplicate checks:**\n    - Compute `householdId` = SHA-256(lastName|postcode) prefix.\n    - **Duplicate identity** (`rejectDuplicateIdentity`) \u2014 key `telephone|email|householdId` against active owners \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` **409**.\n    - **Duplicate household** (`rejectDuplicateHousehold`) \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold`, same `householdId` on an active owner \u2192 `DuplicateHouseholdException` **409**.\n    - **Possible-duplicate soft match** (`findPossibleDuplicateOf`) \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold`, same last name + postcode + different phone \u2192 records lowest matching id (no rejection).\n13. **Entity mapping** \u2014 `ownerMapper.toOwner(dto)` (ignores derived fields, set next).\n14. **Derived fields set on the entity:** `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf`; `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` with collision de-duplication; `householdId`; `householdSize`; `namesakeCount` (same first+last); `bulkSignupWarning` (> 80 that day).\n15. **Persist** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`, `@Transactional` (transaction boundary) \u2192 `ownerRepository.save` (`persist`/`merge`). On Hibernate flush, the entity's own constraints re-validate: `Owner` `@NotEmpty` address/city/telephone + `@Pattern(^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$)` telephone; `Person` `@NotEmpty` firstName/lastName.\n16. **Record idempotency key** \u2014 if supplied, stores `key \u2192 owner.id`. *(side-effect)*\n17. **Audit log** \u2014 INFO line on the `AUDIT` logger (id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel, membershipNumber). *(side-effect)*\n18. **Response** \u2014 map to `OwnerDto` (computes read-only derived fields), set `Location: /api/owners/{id}`, return **201 CREATED**.\n\n## Notes worth flagging\n- **No JPA lifecycle callbacks or events** fire: no `@PrePersist`/`@PostPersist`, no `@EntityListeners`, no `@EventListener`/`@TransactionalEventListener`, no `@PostConstruct`. The only cross-cutting aspect is `CallMonitoringAspect` (JMX call counting \u2014 no business effect).\n- **No email/notification/external calls** anywhere in the path \u2014 the only side channels are the audit log line and the JMX counter.\n- Steps 7, 8, 12, and 14 each trigger their own `findAllOwners()` full scan, so a single create performs several full-table reads before the write.\n- `DuplicateTelephoneException`/`DuplicateEmailException` still have handlers but are **no longer thrown** in the create path \u2014 those checks were folded into the single identity-key check (step 12).\n\nNothing was changed \u2014 this is read-only analysis."
